{{Quote|Orders direct from the fleet&mdash;Mon Mothma's asked you to retrieve logs of Imperial communications that were intercepted by several rebel cells along the Shipwrights' Trace.|[[Arhul Narra]], to Luke Skywalker|<ref name="Weapon" />}}
The '''Shipwrights' Trace''' was a [[hyperspace route]] situated between the astronomical objects [[Fondor]] and [[Allanteen VI]],<ref name="Map" /> running near the [[planet]] [[Quarzite]].<ref name="BMF 66">{{BuildFalconCite|66|Guide to the Galaxy}}</ref> From Fondor located in the [[Colonies]] region, it ran to [[Foless]] on the [[Corellian Trade Spine]]<ref name="TFABG">[[Star Wars: The Force Awakens Beginner Game|''Star Wars: The Force Awakens'' Beginner Game]]</ref> [[super-hyperroute]],<ref name="BMF 48">{{BuildFalconCite|48|Guide to the Galaxy}}</ref> the route went into the [[Inner Rim Territories]] to the celestial body [[Atzerri]] and then the astronomical body [[Chardaan]],<ref name="TFABG" /> located in the [[Chardaan system]]<ref name="Systems" /> along the [[Hydian Way]]<ref name="TFABG" /> super-hyperroute.<ref name="BMF 48" /> The route then went into the [[Expansion Region]] to the<ref name="TFABG" /> [[planet]]<ref name="On the Front Lines">''[[Star Wars: On the Front Lines]]''</ref> [[Tynna]] and then to Allanteen VI, which lay on the [[Corellian Run]]<ref name="TFABG" /> super-hyperroute.<ref name="BMF 48" /> The planet [[Whiforla II]] was located along the Shipwrights' Trace.<ref name="Weapon" />

During the [[Early rebellion against the Galactic Empire|early rebellion]] against the [[Galactic Empire]], the [[Deep Fathom|Deep Current]], an information-gathering resistance group based around Tynna, operated along the Shipwrights' Trace.<ref name="Rebel Files">''[[Star Wars: The Rebel Files]]''</ref> During the [[Galactic Civil War]] between the Rebel Alliance and the [[Galactic Empire]], Alliance [[Chancellor (Rebel Alliance)|Chancellor]] [[Mon Mothma]] tasked the operative [[Luke Skywalker]] with retrieving logs of Imperial communications that were intercepted by rebel cells operating along the Shipwrights' Trace.<ref name="Weapon" />

==Behind the scenes==
The Shipwrights' Trace was first mentioned in [[canon]] in the [[2015]] junior novel ''[[The Weapon of a Jedi: A Luke Skywalker Adventure]]'', written by [[Jason Fry]].<ref name="Weapon" />

